severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the precedence rule when both `uvicorn_backstop_seconds` and `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` are supplied to `run_http_with_grace` (e.g. the explicit back-compat name wins if given, else the preferred name, else the default constant), so the value passed to `timeout_graceful_shutdown` is deterministic.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC bullet 3: 'run_http_with_grace passes uvicorn timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(uvicorn_backstop_seconds)'","AC bullet 4: 'preserves the existing keyword uvicorn_graceful_seconds as a backward-compatible override for callers'","Current signature (src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:102) has a single `uvicorn_graceful_seconds: float = DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS`; the plan splits this into two defaulted parameters without a resolution rule."],"finding":"The plan introduces two live keyword parameters that both feed uvicorn's timeout_graceful_shutdown — the new preferred `uvicorn_backstop_seconds` and the back-compat `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` — but never specifies which wins when a caller supplies both, leaving the value that reaches `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(...)` undefined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f17f1fe30fa0c87b8","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (bullets 3 and 4): 'passes uvicorn timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(uvicorn_backstop_seconds)' vs 'preserves the existing keyword uvicorn_graceful_seconds as a backward-compatible override'","norm_id":"n0d8f6bb2482b004f","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller (or a test) passes both uvicorn_backstop_seconds and uvicorn_graceful_seconds with different values","A future caller migrating to the new name sets uvicorn_backstop_seconds while a wrapper still forwards the old uvicorn_graceful_seconds default"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Make `uvicorn_backstop_seconds` default to a sentinel (None) and `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` also default to None; resolve as `effective = uvicorn_graceful_seconds if uvicorn_graceful_seconds is not None else (uvicorn_backstop_seconds if uvicorn_backstop_seconds is not None else DEFAULT_UVICORN_BACKSTOP_SECONDS)`, and add an AC asserting the resolved value when both are passed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an AC that the deadline-elapse shutdown path emits a distinct log/metric (e.g. gauge-busy-at-deadline) so operators can observe when the certified-op drain deadline forced exit versus the idle early-exit path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'if the certified-op drain deadline expires while the gauge is